<title>JAPAN: Tokyo Grain Exchange names Kawamura acting chief.</title>
<headline>Tokyo Grain Exchange names Kawamura acting chief.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tokyo Grain Exchange (TGE) said on Monday that senior managing director Katsumi Kawamura has been named acting president after the death of Seiji Mori at the weekend.</p>
<p>The TGE said earlier on Monday that Mori, 72, died of cancer.</p>
<p>Mori, a former Agriculture Ministry official, took over as president in May 1989 and was behind the launching of a yen-based corn futures contract in 1992 and a U.S. soybean futures option contract in 1991.</p>
</text>
